{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582920552,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffeA6T6YnPwZlkW2y","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57a3423001Y9pEG8pYg568Qe","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d0ffeA6T6YnPwZlkW2y","messageID":"msg_1d57a28d600100iV7cYJORm8Wp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a0128bfd40f983","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","newString":"- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.","oldString":"- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it."},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -96,9 +96,9 @@\n \n - Flags: `node measure-brief-cost.mjs [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` keeps every typed row on the `none` split, `--rows` narrows the run to named corpus ids and `--root` names the checkout the corpus and hook are read from, defaulting to the current directory. A holdout or unknown id exits 2 before anything is spawned, and no prompt is ever printed.\n - Output keys: one JSON object holds `rows`, then `liveRows`, `totalBytes`, `medianBytes`, `maxBytes`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes`. Each entry of `rows` carries `id`, `bytes`, `headBytes`, `estimatedTokens` and `live`, where bytes are the UTF-8 length of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`, headBytes is the UTF-8 length of its first line, live says whether that first line starts `Advisor: live`, and tokens divide the context bytes by four, the renderer's own characters per token. Every byte statistic is taken over live rows only.\n - Refusal: a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor.\n-- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n+- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\n \n ---\n \n ## 4. STRUCTURE\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\", \"newString\": \"- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\", \"oldString\": \"- Sandbox: the run makes one `ssa-cost-` directory under the OS temp dir and sets `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to it for every hook process, so the operator's warm daemon is never reached. At the end it stops only a process whose command line names that directory and removes it.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582918179,"end":1794582920552}}}}
